    - {fileID: 21300000, guid: 26a4aa98be8fb6e4999afef33fd15887, type: 3}
    titleName: 
    description: "Central Processing Unit (CPU)\r\nCommonly known as the CPU or processor,
      this is the brain of the computer. It interprets and carries out the basic
      instructions to operate a computer. \r\nIt impacts overall computing power
      and manages most of the computer operations. The motherboard contains a socket
      to hold the processor or CPU. The central processing unit (CPU), also called
      the processor or microprocessor, does most of the processing of data and instructions
      for the entire system. Because the CPU generates heat, a fan and heat sink
      might be installed on top to keep it cool.\r\nNowadays, processors have multiple
      cores called multi-core processors. This means that the processor is a single
      chips that has two or more separate processors. In multi-core processors, each
      of the processors run at a slower clock speed as compared to a single-core
      processor, but this efficient process typically increases performance. There
      are two kinds of common multi-core processors today:\r\n1.     Dual Core Processor
      \u2013 chip that contains two separate processors\r\n2.     Quad Core Processor
      \u2013 chip with four separate processors\n\n\nAMD and Intel are the two most
      popular brands of processors in the market nowadays.\r\nBundled with the processors
      are the heat sinks.  A heat sink consists of metal fins that draw heat away
      from a component. The fan and heat sink together are called the processor cooler.
      The photo below shows a CPU with a heat sink mounted on the motherboard.\r\n\r\n"
    has3dView: 1
  - contentName: 0
    modelName: 0
    display:
    - {fileID: 21300000, guid: 8758bd2176ba76b4db94244245ed097a, type: 3}
    - {fileID: 21300000, guid: 752f59a543746f84aaed56ce9d59583a, type: 3}
    titleName: 'Cooling Technology

'
    description: "Cooling technologies are essential in avoiding the computer from
      overheating and maintaining a good, well-ventilated system.\n\nSeveral cooling
      technologies are present throughout the system unit:\r\n o    Fans are also
      present in several components such as the power supply, ports, processor, hard
      disk etc.\r\no    Heat sink, on another hand, is a small metal or ceramic component
      with fins on the surface which absorbs and distributes heat produced by electrical
      components.\r\no    Heat pipe is used on smaller devices like notebook computers
      since this is smaller in size.\r\n\r\n"
    has3dView: 1
  - contentName: 0
    modelName: 0
    display:
    - {fileID: 21300000, guid: b427f0da091c09742a128a81485de5e5, type: 3}
    - {fileID: 21300000, guid: b404d2289d1401f4b94a0f5ae0932ac3, type: 3}
    titleName: 'Cables

'
    description: "There are two main types of computer cables: a data cable and a
      power cable.\r\n A data cable is a cable that provides communication between
      devices. For example, the data cable (i.e., DVI, HDMI, or VGA) that connects
      your monitor to your computer to create a picture on the monitor. Other popular
      examples of data cables include the CAT5, IDE/EIDE, SATA, and USB cables.\r\n\n\n
      A power cable is any cable that powers the device. For example, the power cord
      that connects to your computer and a Molex cable inside the computer are examples
      of power cables.\r\n"
    has3dView: 0
